 "story": "Liverpool beat Club Brugge 3-0 at the Jan Breydel Stadium, a win that left them fifth in the Champions League table. Alexander Isak gave Liverpool the lead in the 13th minute, set up by Dominik Szoboszlai. Liverpool led 1-0 at half-time. Florian Wirtz made it 2-0 in the 79th minute from a pass by Rio Ngumoha, who had come off the bench for Víctor Muñoz. Isak scored his second three minutes later, with Alisson Becker providing the assist, to make it 3-0. Club Brugge had 53.5% of the possession and 17 shots to Liverpool's 13, and Liverpool made five saves to their one.",
